0..75 Comment "// A function reads a module\'s signature as a value and a model through its"
76..84 Comment "// type."
85..87 Comment "//"
88..162 Comment "// A render over a module reads both parts. The presentation of a `theory`"
163..237 Comment "// block is a `Theory` value, so an ordinary function folds a signature. A"
238..314 Comment "// model is a record at `Model(T)`, so a function reads each field it names."
315..317 Comment "//"
318..392 Comment "// `declared` folds `std.build`\'s `Gandr.Package` into eleven constants at"
393..470 Comment "// `String`. The members of the theories it includes come first, in the order"
471..548 Comment "// of its `include` lines. `toolchain` reads the content fields of a model by"
549..564 Comment "// their names."
565..567 Comment "//"
568..583 Comment "// - see: #4730"
584..676 Comment "// - see: `../../pathological/desc/module-reflection.gandr` — what does not reach a module"
